  "structuralRules": [
    "Every record is tenant-private and binds one exact run, one exact immutable Part 2A policy version and at least one exact source snapshot.",
    "Every non-root record names each direct parent by record identity, record type and canonical record digest.",
    "A parent from another tenant or policy, a stale digest, a missing parent, a duplicate parent, a disallowed parent type or a non-lower ordinal fails closed.",
    "Eligibility, proposal, approval, schedule, action unit, attempt, acknowledgement, delivery, response, task, suppression, cancellation, reconciliation and terminal outcome are never represented by one conflated record.",
    "A provider attempt is the only record class that may describe an attempted external effect; it is not acknowledgement, delivery, reply, payment, collection or success.",
    "Evidence records cannot create or retroactively widen action authority, mutate upstream truth, move money, or claim a stronger state than authenticated evidence.",
    "Corrections, suppression, cancellation and reconciliation append records; they never mutate or erase prior intent, attempts or evidence.",
    "Terminal outcome is an automation endpoint only and must identify unresolved uncertainty rather than convert it to success."
  ],
